description: Keep live API hosts out of git; load them from local env.
alwaysApply: true
---

# API host and paths are secrets-in-repo

This repo is public. Do **not** put the live API hostname or real endpoint paths in committed files.

## Must

- Read the host only via `ApiConfig` (`lib/data/api/api_config.dart`).
- Read paths only via `ApiEndpoints` (`lib/data/api/api_endpoints.dart`) using `String.fromEnvironment`.
- Store real values in local `.env` (`API_BASE_URL` with no trailing slash; `API_PATH_*` keys from `.env.example`).
- Run / build with `--dart-define-from-file=.env`.
- Keep `.env` gitignored. Commit `.env.example` with empty values.
- GitHub Actions: one repository secret per `.env` key (`API_BASE_URL`, `API_PATH_*`). Workflow writes the gitignored `.env`, then `--dart-define-from-file=.env`.

## Must not

- Hardcode `https://…` API hosts or real path strings in Dart, tests, README, PROJECT.md, CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, or rules.
- Describe APIs, servers, hosts, or endpoints in any `*.md` file (this repo is public).
- Commit `.env`, `api.md` dumps, or cURL samples that include the real host or paths.
- Bundle `.env` as a Flutter asset (`flutter_dotenv` in `pubspec` assets).
- Print `ApiConfig.baseUrl` or `ApiEndpoints` values in logs, crash reports, or UI.

## Example

```dart
// BAD
final uri = Uri.parse('https://example-live-host/api/your_routine');

// GOOD
final uri = ApiConfig.uri(ApiEndpoints.schedule);
```

```bash
flutter run --dart-define-from-file=.env
flutter test --dart-define-from-file=.env
```
